        },
        {
          "name": "Archer",
          "expression": "neutral",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "Orléans, spring 1429",
      "narration": "Spring, 1429. For six grueling months, the English army has strangled the French city of Orléans. If Orléans falls, the road into the heart of France lies wide open—and the kingdom is finished.",
      "word_count": 33
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-02",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "Hook",
      "start": 56,
      "duration": 15,
      "image": "images/shot-02.png",
      "background": "hall",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Charles",
          "expression": "closed",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "Meanwhile, France's future king is hiding out in a castle far to the south. He's broke, out of allies, and hasn't even been officially crowned. Some days, he isn't even sure he's the rightful heir.",
      "word_count": 35
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-03",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "Hook",
      "start": 71,
      "duration": 12,
      "image": "images/shot-03.png",
      "background": "village",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Joan",
          "expression": "determined",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "Hope is dead. Until, out of nowhere, an illiterate teenage farm girl shows up at the gates, claiming God sent her to save the entire country.",
      "word_count": 26
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-04",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "France on the brink",
      "start": 83,
      "duration": 15,
      "image": "images/shot-04.png",
      "background": "parchment",
      "camera": "static",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "English knight",
          "expression": "smug",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "French knight",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "Treaty of Troyes, 1420",
      "narration": "Remember the brutal English victory at Agincourt? The treaty that followed basically handed the French crown to England. When both kings died in 1422, the English declared King Henry's infant son ruler of both nations.",
      "word_count": 35
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-05",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "France on the brink",
      "start": 98,
      "duration": 16,
      "image": "images/shot-05.png",
      "background": "parchment",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "English knight",
          "expression": "smug",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Burgundian knight",
          "expression": "smug",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Charles",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "French knight",
          "expression": "determined",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "With their powerful allies, the Dukes of Burgundy, England controlled Paris and almost all of northern France. Down south sat Charles, the French king's son. People called him the Dauphin—the heir—because he still hadn't been crowned.",
      "word_count": 36
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-06",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "France on the brink",
      "start": 114,
      "duration": 16,
      "image": "images/shot-06.png",
      "background": "cathedral",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [],
      "on_screen_text": "Reims",
      "narration": "By tradition, French kings had to be crowned in the cathedral of Reims. The problem? Reims was buried deep inside enemy territory. Without that crown, half the country didn't even see Charles as a real king.",
      "word_count": 36
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-07",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "France on the brink",
      "start": 130,
      "duration": 12,
      "image": "images/shot-07.png",
      "background": "siege",
      "camera": "slow pan left",
      "characters": [],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "In October 1428, the English tightened the noose, laying siege to Orléans—the last major fortress blocking their path south. Month after month, the city held on. Barely.",
      "word_count": 27
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-08",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The girl from Domrémy",
      "start": 142,
      "duration": 18,
      "image": "images/shot-08.png",
      "background": "village",
      "camera": "slow pan right",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Father",
          "expression": "gentle",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Joan",
          "expression": "gentle",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Mother",
          "expression": "gentle",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "Domrémy, around 1412",
      "narration": "Far to the east, in a quiet village called Domrémy, lived a peasant girl named Jeanne—known in English as Joan. She spent her days farming, herding sheep, and praying. She couldn't read. She couldn't write. She had never held a sword.",
      "word_count": 41
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-09",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The girl from Domrémy",
      "start": 160,
      "duration": 12,
      "image": "images/shot-09.png",
      "background": "village",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Joan",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "Around age thirteen, Joan claimed she began hearing voices—saints sent directly by God. At first, the voices just told her to be kind and go to church.",
      "word_count": 27
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-10",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The girl from Domrémy",
      "start": 172,
      "duration": 12,
      "image": "images/shot-10.png",
      "background": "village",
      "camera": "quick push in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Joan",
          "expression": "determined",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "Then, the message changed. They commanded her to leave home, drive the English out of France, and march the Dauphin to Reims to claim his crown.",
      "word_count": 26
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-11",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The girl from Domrémy",
      "start": 184,
      "duration": 19,
      "image": "images/shot-11.png",
      "background": "hall",
      "camera": "static",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Joan",
          "expression": "gentle",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Baudricourt",
          "expression": "smug",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "Robert de Baudricourt",
      "narration": "At sixteen, she walked to a nearby garrison and asked the local commander, Robert de Baudricourt, for an armed escort to see the prince. He laughed in her face and told her family to take her home and slap some sense into her.",
      "word_count": 43
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-12",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The girl from Domrémy",
      "start": 203,
      "duration": 12,
      "image": "images/shot-12.png",
      "background": "hall",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Joan",
          "expression": "determined",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Baudricourt",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "She came back. And kept coming back. Finally, the commander relented—rumor has it, after Joan accurately predicted a major French defeat days before the messenger even arrived.",
      "word_count": 27
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-13",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The road to Chinon",
      "start": 215,
      "duration": 13,
      "image": "images/shot-13.png",
      "background": "river",
      "camera": "track left",
      "characters": [
