        },
        {
          "name": "Soldier",
          "expression": "determined",
          "pose": "walk"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "11 days through enemy land",
      "narration": "In February 1429, Joan cut her hair short, put on men's riding clothes, and rode for eleven dangerous days straight through enemy-held territory with just a handful of guards.",
      "word_count": 29
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-14",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The road to Chinon",
      "start": 228,
      "duration": 21,
      "image": "images/shot-14.png",
      "background": "hall",
      "camera": "slow pan right",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Courtier",
          "expression": "smug",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Charles",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Joan",
          "expression": "gentle",
          "pose": "bow"
        },
        {
          "name": "Courtier",
          "expression": "smug",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "Chinon",
      "narration": "When she reached the castle of Chinon, legend says Charles decided to test her. He disguised himself in plain clothes and hid among his nobles while someone else sat on the throne. Joan walked right past the decoy, straight into the crowd, and knelt before the real Dauphin.",
      "word_count": 48
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-15",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The road to Chinon",
      "start": 249,
      "duration": 17,
      "image": "images/shot-15.png",
      "background": "hall",
      "camera": "static",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Churchman",
          "expression": "neutral",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Churchman",
          "expression": "neutral",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Joan",
          "expression": "gentle",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "Still, Charles wasn't about to bet his kingdom on a miracle. For weeks, top churchmen interrogated Joan, looking for any sign of heresy or madness. They found nothing—only fierce devotion. And frankly, Charles had nothing left to lose.",
      "word_count": 38
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-16",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The road to Chinon",
      "start": 266,
      "duration": 21,
      "image": "images/shot-16.png",
      "background": "hall",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Joan",
          "expression": "determined",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "\"Forty times more than my sword\"",
      "narration": "So he gave her a suit of white armor, a warhorse, and a spot in the relief army marching to Orléans. Instead of leading with a weapon, Joan carried a white banner covered in golden lilies. She later admitted she loved that banner forty times more than her sword.",
      "word_count": 49
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-17",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "Orléans",
      "start": 287,
      "duration": 9,
      "image": "images/shot-17.png",
      "background": "siege",
      "camera": "slow pan left",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Townsman",
          "expression": "gentle",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Townsman",
          "expression": "gentle",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Joan",
          "expression": "gentle",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "29 April 1429",
      "narration": "Joan rode into Orléans at the end of April. Starving, desperate citizens flooded the streets just to touch her armor.",
      "word_count": 20
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-18",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "Orléans",
      "start": 296,
      "duration": 19,
      "image": "images/shot-18.png",
      "background": "siege",
      "camera": "static",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Commander",
          "expression": "smug",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Commander",
          "expression": "angry",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Joan",
          "expression": "determined",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "The seasoned French generals, however, treated her like a mascot. They locked her out of war councils and launched attacks without telling her. So Joan simply grabbed her banner, rode straight to the front lines, and the common soldiers followed her into hell.",
      "word_count": 43
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-19",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "Orléans",
      "start": 315,
      "duration": 13,
      "image": "images/shot-19.png",
      "background": "siege",
      "camera": "shake",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Joan",
          "expression": "closed",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "French knight",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "walk"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "7 May 1429",
      "narration": "On May 7th, while storming a heavily fortified English stronghold, an arrow pierced Joan right between her neck and shoulder. Badly wounded, she was dragged away from the battle.",
      "word_count": 29
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-20",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "Orléans",
      "start": 328,
      "duration": 17,
      "image": "images/shot-20.png",
      "background": "siege",
      "camera": "quick push in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Joan",
          "expression": "angry",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "French knight",
          "expression": "angry",
          "pose": "walk"
        },
        {
          "name": "French knight",
          "expression": "angry",
          "pose": "walk"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "Hours later, against all medical logic, she pulled the arrow out, got back on her horse, and charged back into the smoke waving her banner. Seeing her alive terrified the English—and electrified the French. They took the fortress.",
      "word_count": 38
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-21",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "Orléans",
      "start": 345,
      "duration": 12,
      "image": "images/shot-21.png",
      "background": "siege",
      "camera": "slow zoom out",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "English knight",
          "expression": "closed",
          "pose": "walk"
        },
        {
          "name": "Archer",
          "expression": "closed",
          "pose": "walk"
        },
        {
          "name": "Joan",
          "expression": "gentle",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "Siege broken in 9 days",
      "narration": "The very next morning, the English army packed up and retreated. A siege that had choked Orléans for over six months was shattered in just nine days.",
      "word_count": 27
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-22",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The tide turns",
      "start": 357,
      "duration": 9,
      "image": "images/shot-22.png",
