        },
        {
          "name": "Joan",
          "expression": "gentle",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "Reims, 17 July 1429",
      "narration": "On July 17, 1429, Charles was finally crowned King Charles VII of France inside Reims Cathedral. Standing right beside the high altar was Joan, holding her white banner high.",
      "word_count": 29
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-27",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The crown at Reims",
      "start": 422,
      "duration": 16,
      "image": "images/shot-27.png",
      "background": "cathedral",
      "camera": "quick push in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Joan",
          "expression": "gentle",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "\"It had borne the burden\"",
      "narration": "When critics later asked why her battle flag was allowed at such a sacred ceremony, Joan gave a simple answer: \"It had borne the burden, so it was only right that it should share the honor.\"",
      "word_count": 36
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-28",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "Captured",
      "start": 438,
      "duration": 19,
      "image": "images/shot-28.png",
      "background": "hall",
      "camera": "static",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Joan",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "King",
          "expression": "closed",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "Joan had kept her promise. She wanted to keep pushing and take back Paris—but King Charles had lost his nerve. Now that he had his crown, he preferred slow diplomacy over war. An attack on Paris stalled, and Joan was wounded once again.",
      "word_count": 43
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-29",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "Captured",
      "start": 457,
      "duration": 11,
      "image": "images/shot-29.png",
