        },
        {
          "name": "Joan",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Burgundian knight",
          "expression": "angry",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "Compiègne, May 1430",
      "narration": "In May 1430, while fighting a rearguard action to defend the town of Compiègne, Joan was dragged off her horse and captured by Burgundian troops.",
      "word_count": 25
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-30",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "Captured",
      "start": 468,
      "duration": 14,
      "image": "images/shot-30.png",
      "background": "hall",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Burgundian knight",
          "expression": "smug",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "English knight",
          "expression": "smug",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "King",
          "expression": "closed",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "They sold her to the English for a king's ransom. And King Charles—the man who owed his throne to this teenage girl—didn't pay a single coin to save her. He didn't even try.",
      "word_count": 33
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-31",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The trial",
      "start": 482,
      "duration": 14,
      "image": "images/shot-31.png",
      "background": "court",
