      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "English knight",
          "expression": "smug",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Joan",
          "expression": "neutral",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "Rouen, 1431",
      "narration": "The English didn't just want Joan dead; they wanted her ruined. If they could prove she was a witch or a heretic, then Charles had been crowned by the devil—making his kingship worthless.",
      "word_count": 33
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-32",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The trial",
      "start": 496,
      "duration": 11,
      "image": "images/shot-32.png",
      "background": "court",
      "camera": "static",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Churchman",
          "expression": "neutral",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Cauchon",
          "expression": "angry",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Churchman",
          "expression": "neutral",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "Bishop Pierre Cauchon",
      "narration": "In 1431, in the English-held city of Rouen, Joan was dragged before a rigged church court led by Bishop Pierre Cauchon, an English loyalist.",
      "word_count": 24
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-33",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The trial",
      "start": 507,
      "duration": 27,
      "image": "images/shot-33.png",
      "background": "court",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Cauchon",
          "expression": "smug",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Joan",
          "expression": "neutral",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "For months, dozens of highly educated scholars fired complex theological traps at an illiterate nineteen-year-old girl. During one session, a judge asked if she knew she was in God's grace. It was a deadly trap: according to church doctrine, no one could know that for sure. Say yes, and she was guilty of heresy; say no, and she confessed to being a sinner.",
      "word_count": 63
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-34",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The trial",
      "start": 534,
      "duration": 17,
      "image": "images/shot-34.png",
      "background": "court",
      "camera": "quick push in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Joan",
          "expression": "gentle",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "\"If I am not, may God put me there\"",
      "narration": "Joan didn't blink. She replied: \"If I am not, may God put me there; and if I am, may God so keep me.\" The courtroom went dead silent. The scribes didn't even know what to write down.",
      "word_count": 37
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-35",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The trial",
      "start": 551,
      "duration": 12,
      "image": "images/shot-35.png",
      "background": "court",
      "camera": "static",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Cauchon",
          "expression": "angry",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Joan",
          "expression": "closed",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "Still, the verdict had been decided before the trial even began. She was found guilty of heresy—and of refusing to stop wearing men's clothing in prison.",
      "word_count": 26
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-36",
      "speaker": null,
      "lead": 2.5,
      "section": "The darkest day",
      "start": 563,
      "duration": 13,
